<title>USA: Oregon $27 mln deal repriced, top yield six pct.</title>
<headline>Oregon $27 mln deal repriced, top yield six pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Wednesday it repriced Oregon's $27.3 million Housing and Community Services Department bond deal. The top yield at the repricing was six percent in 2027.</p>
<p>The repricing scale follows:  </p>
<p>STATE OF OREGON</p>
<p>RE: $27,300,000*</p>
<p>HOUSING AND COMMUNITY SERVICES DEPARTMENT</p>
<p>MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(SINGLE-FAMILY MORTGAGE PROGRAM)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD AT THE FOLLOWING REPRICE IN THE 1998-2004</p>
<p>MATURITIES.</p>
<p>WRITTEN AWARD EXPECTED THURSDAY, NOVEMBER 21, 1996.</p>
<p>					    27,300,000*</p>
<p>					   1996 SERIES H</p>
